Yes, you can visualize the resulting edge image in Matlab using the `imshow` function. Here's an example code:

```
% Read the original image
originalImage = imread('example.jpg');

% Perform Canny edge detection
lowThreshold = 0.1; % adjust as needed
highThreshold = 0.3; % adjust as needed
sigma = 1; % adjust as needed
edgeImage = edge(originalImage, 'canny', [lowThreshold highThreshold], sigma);

% Show the original and edge images side by side
subplot(1, 2, 1);
imshow(originalImage);
title('Original Image');
subplot(1, 2, 2);
imshow(edgeImage);
title('Edge Image');
```

This code reads an example image, performs Canny edge detection with some tuning of the `lowThreshold`, `highThreshold`, and `sigma` parameters, and then displays the original and edge images side by side in a single figure window using the `subplot` and `imshow` functions.
